addit Pontacus causas in notis. Sed et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pelopem</HI> 
ille subjungit Euristheo, quem tamen non
diffitetur ab aliis omitti, qui  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pevlopoû mnhvmhn oujd1 oålwû</FOREIGN> 
faciunt: in eaque erat Eusebius sententia. In Agamemnonis
quoque, et Orestis annis nonnihil dissentit,
quod in Chronico suis quaeque locis edisseremus.
Demum nec satis bene  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Penqeuúû</FOREIGN>  ei dicitur, quem cum
Latino Laterculo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pevnqilon</FOREIGN>  vocat et Pausanias in Corinthiacis
cap. 18.</NOTE></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><COL N="0086C"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujrusqeuúû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Atreuúû kaiú Quevsthû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xe'</FOREIGN></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Agamevmnwn</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ih'</FOREIGN></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><COL N="0087A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aiægisqoû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eåth e'</FOREIGN></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Orevsthû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kg'</FOREIGN></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Tisamenoúû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Penqeuúû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Komivthû</FOREIGN></GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Meq1 ouÝû 2Hrakleidwðn kaqodoû</FOREIGN> .</GL.TERM> <GL.GLOSS></GL.GLOSS></LIST.GL> <LIST.GL COM="0087"><HEAD COM="0087"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>KORIäNQIWN</FOREIGN> .</HEAD> <GL.TERM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Alhvthû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0087" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0087B"></COL> Graeca ex Syncello pag. 144, de more huc transtulimus.
