 <NOTE N="d" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314B"></COL> Qui  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kavspoû Silouviçoû</FOREIGN>  Syncello appellatur, nono
donatur loco, annisque regni  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>la'.</FOREIGN>  Attamen et in
primo Palatino ms.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Caspis</HI>  dicitur, plerisque aliis
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Capys.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kavpau</FOREIGN>  vocat Strabo, quem et Capuae
conditorem facit. Scaliger hanc subsequenti periochae
ita nectit uno sensu,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Capis Silvius Attii superioris
regis filius, annis</HI>  28. Sed illud additum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Silvius,</HI> 
libri non pauci ignorant: alterum vero  <HI REND="ITALIC">Attii</HI>  nomen
ne unus quidem, quem scio, habet.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">SYLVIUS,
