40. (1 to 4)</HEAD> <P COM="0475"></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0475" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0475"><HI REND="ITALIC">Macedon.</HI>  (11 to 12)</HEAD> <P COM="0475"></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0475" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0475"><HI REND="ITALIC">Macedon.
XXV, PHILIPPUS,
qui et Aridaeus,
frater
Alexandri,
an.</HI>  7. (1 to 4)</HEAD> <P COM="0475"></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0475" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0475"><HI REND="ITALIC">Romanorum.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0475">Harpalus fugit <NOTE N="a" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0475" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0475A"></COL> Rescripsimus  <HI REND="ITALIC">in Atticam,</HI>  ipso admonente in curis
posterioribus Pontaco, cum antea perperam  <HI REND="ITALIC">in
Asiam</HI>  legeretur etiam apud Scaligerum, cui tamen
ipsa illa emendatio loci suboluit. Quae subnectuntur
de victis Samnitibus hoc numero probe convenire,
ipse demum Scaliger non diffitetur. Caetera confer
Sigonium.</NOTE>  in Atticam.</P> <P COM="0475">Romani Samnites subigunt, et colonias deducunt.</P> <P COM="0475">Alexander <NOTE N="b" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0475" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0475A"></COL> Superaddendi sunt septem aut octo menses ex
aliorum auctorum consensu; nam et obiisse Alexandrum
 <COL N="0475B"></COL> olympiad. 114, inquit Josephus contra Appion.
lib. I,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnteû oJmologouðsi.</FOREIGN>  Rectius proinde legi videtur
in primo Palat. ms. 33 pro 32, ut et  <HI REND="ITALIC">in Babylone</HI>  cum
libris plerisque aliis, pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">apud Babylonem</HI>  Scaligeri.
Neque obstat quod Dexippus Syncello laudatus vicesimo
aetatis suae anno imperium suscepisse Alexandrum
tradit, et quod duodecim annos regnasse, communis
opinio sit: Diodorus quippe, Arrianus atque
alii menses illos  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJptaú,</FOREIGN>  aut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojktwú</FOREIGN>  regni annis adjiciunt.
Ad haec Schurzfleischius ait: Malala; e Theophilo
chronographo p. 248:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Alevxandroû,</FOREIGN>  inquit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæzhse
meún eæth l¾', ejbasivleuse deú uJpotavxaû taú pavnta, eæth iz'.</FOREIGN> 
Nicephorus Syncello adjectus, p. 399:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Alevxandroû,</FOREIGN> 
ait,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaqelwún thún twún Perswðn ajrchún, ejbasivleusen eæth ¾'</FOREIGN> 
(sic vetus chronographus, qui sub Severo scripsit,
apud H. Canisium tom. II antiq. Lect. p. 600, Alexandrum
post mortem Darii annis circiter septem
imperasse, docuit),  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proú touð kaqeleiðn toún Dareiðon basileuvsaû,
fasiún, eæth ib' kaiú ejteleuvthsen ejn Babulwðni, wJû
fasin, ejtwðn le', wJû deú aælloi, ejtwðn l¾'.</FOREIGN>  Haec omnia
multo distant intervallo ab Eusebio, quem tamen sequitur
Cedrenus, qui,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú oJ meún ejpiú tosouvtoiû,</FOREIGN>  infit,
 <COL N="0476A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katorqwvmasi toún bivon methvllaxe, dusiú kaiú devka crovnoiû,
proúû mhsiún eåx, toiðû ajrchðû ajpolauvsaû, biwvsaû deú taú
pavnta eæth duvo kaiú triavkonta.</FOREIGN>  Annos 12 eum regnasse,
plurimi auctores consentiunt, Eratosthenes puta
apud Clementem Alexand. Strom. I, Tertullianus
contra Judaeos, Joseph. Antiquit. lib. XII c. 2, I Machab.
I, comm. 8, Orosius lib. III c. 23, aliique, Eusebium
secuti. Suidas tamen his verbis aliter sentit:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Alevxandroû, oJ Filivppou kaiú 1Olumpiavdoû, basileuvsaû Makedovnwn
ejniautwðn ih', teleuthvsaû deú ejtwðn lg'.</FOREIGN>  Ex hoc
loco possit primi Palatini lectio defendi, a qua nec
abludit Arrianus, qui,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn toiðû kat1 1Alevxandron,</FOREIGN>  lib. VII
fine,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejbivw deú</FOREIGN>  ait,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>duvo kaiú triavkonta eæth, kaiú touð trivtou
mhðnaû ejpevlaben ojktwú, ejbasivleuse deú touvtwn touúû te
ojktwú mhðnaû, kaiú eæth ib'.</FOREIGN>  Qui plures veterum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>diafwnivaû</FOREIGN> 
de his rebus nosse cupit, addat Stephanum
Episc. Oriol. comment. ad c. I lib. I Machabaeorum,
et, qui ex illo auctoris Machabaeorum libri loco
Alexandrum per 24 annos Macedoniae imperasse
contendit, Joannem Harduinum, Chronol. V. T.
 <COL N="0476B"></COL> pag. 162. Vide et Samuel Petitum ad LL. Atticas
pag. 257.</NOTE>  33 aetatis suae anno moritur in Babylone, post quem translato in
multos imperio, diversi regnaverunt.</P> <P COM="0475">Lydiam, <NOTE N="c" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0476" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0476B"></COL> Notatum ante nos Scaligero ex Diodori lib. XVIII,
Thraciam quidem Lysimacho, non vero Lydiam, quae
Meleagro tradita est, obtigisse. Historia in Veterum
scriptis notissima.</NOTE>  et Thraciam, et Hellespontum Lysimachus tenuit.</P> <P COM="0475">Appius <NOTE N="d" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0476" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0476B"></COL> Hanc Scaliger periocham proxime superiori praeposuit.
Non autem diffiteor satius fuisse tempus, quo
Appius Claudius inclaruit, serius assignare, puta ad
olymp. 117 initium, cum censor creatus est, quam
dignitatem, ut Frontinus lib. I de Aquaeductibus
narrat, multis tergiversationibus extraxit, donec et
viam, et aquae ductum perficeret. Auctor libri de
Viris illustribus eum tradit toto quinquennio censuram
continuasse.</NOTE>  Claudius Caecus Romae clarus habetur, qui aquam Claudiam induxit,
et viam Appiam stravit.</P> <P COM="0475">Macedonum duces in seditionem versi.</P> <P COM="0475">Agathocles <NOTE N="e" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0476" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0476B"></COL> Debuit, id ipsum, recte notante Scaligero, gestum
conferri in ultimum subsequentis olymp. annum,
siquidem a Trojae excidio ad annum, qui proxime
praecedit Agathoclis tyrannidem, bene supputat
Diodorus lib. XIX,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæth ojktakosiva ejxhvkonta eJx,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ann.</HI>  866.</NOTE>  Syracusis tyrannidem exercet.</P> <P COM="0475">Lamiacum bellum motum.</P> <P COM="0475">Perdicca adversus Aegyptios dimicat.</P> <P COM="0475">Ptolemaeus Lagi filius Jerosolymis et Judaea in ditionem suam dolo redactis,
plurimos captivorum in Aegyptum transtulit.</P> <P COM="0475">Judaeorum pontifex maximus Onias Jaddi filius clarus habetur.</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0475" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0475"><HI REND="ITALIC">Ann.
ab
Abr.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0475"></P></DIV2> <COL N="0477"></COL> <NOTE TYPE="Fragmenta Graeca" ANCHORED=N BLOCK=YES COM="0477"><COL N="0477"></COL> <P COM="0477"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makedovnwn k¾', ejbasivleuse KASANDROS eæth iq'.</FOREIGN>  Syncell.
pag. 215.</P> 

 <P COM="0477"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mevnandroû oJ kwmikoúû poihthúû prwðton draðgma didavxaû
1Orghún ejnivka.</FOREIGN>  Idem pag. 219.</P> 

 <P COM="0477"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qeovfrastoû filovsofoû ejgnwrivzeto.</FOREIGN>  Idem. ibidem.</P> 

 <P COM="0477"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qeovdwroû oJ aæqeoû ejgnwrivzeto.</FOREIGN>  Idem ibidem.</P> 

 <P COM="0477"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Dhmhvtrioû oJ Falhreuúû ejgnwrivzeto.</FOREIGN>  Idem ibidem.</P> 

